## 8 & 9. Neighbor Expansion — Retrieval Slot vs. Context Assembly Experiment

### A. Neighbor-as-Retrieval (Phase 2 Architecture — HARMFUL)
Placing expanded sibling chunks directly into Top-10 retrieval slots dilutes the Top-10 window with adjacent context, dropping Recall@10 from **42.8% to 12.5% ($\pm 1$) and 8.3% ($\pm 2$)**.

### B. Neighbor-as-Context (Correct Preserved Retrieval Experiment — BENEFICIAL)
Keeping Top-10 retrieval ranking **100% untouched** and appending sibling chunks ($\pm 1$ or $\pm 2$) **ONLY during LLM context assembly** yields:

| Neighbor Context Window | Retrieval Recall@10 | Required Evidence Recovered in Context | Add'l Useful Evidence Chunks | Add'l Irrelevant Chunks | Total Context Chunks | Expansion Ratio |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |
| **Original Top-10 (No Neighbors)** | 42.8% | 16.7% | 0.00 | 0.00 | 10.0 | $1.00\times$ |
| **Context Expansion $\pm 1$** | **42.8%** | **16.7%** | $+0.50$ | $+7.83$ | 29.5 | $2.95\times$ |
| **Context Expansion $\pm 2$** | **42.8%** | **50.0%** | **$+0.83$** | $+17.17$ | 45.7 | $4.57\times$ |

> **Key Discovery**:  
> Neighbor expansion $\pm 2$ as a **context-building mechanism** recovers **50.0% of Required Evidence** (up from 16.7%) without degrading retrieval precision metrics.

