## 16. Controlled Combined Experiment (80/20 RRF + 3-parent Dedup)

Empirical measurement of the combined candidate configuration (`80/20 RRF` + `3 chunks/parent`) yields:

$$\text{Baseline Recall (50.0\%)} \longrightarrow \text{80/20 Recall (55.3\%)} + \text{3-parent Recall (51.9\%)} \longrightarrow \mathbf{\text{Combined Recall (51.9\%)}}$$

* **Interaction Finding**: The combined architecture does **NOT** achieve cumulative additive gains ($57.2\%$). Combining 80/20 RRF with 3-parent deduplication results in **$51.9\%$ Recall@10** and **$0.349$ MRR**.
* **Causal Factor**: 80/20 RRF already heavily concentrates candidates from top vector parents; capping parents at 3 prevents lower-ranked secondary vector hits from surfacing.

---

## 17. Final Decision Framework

1. **Experimentally Supported Observations**:
   * Vector-dominant RRF weighting ($80/20$ or $70/30$) successfully recovers vector hits suppressed by BM25 keyword noise, raising RRF Recall@10 from $50.0\%$ to $55.3\%$ and MRR from $0.263$ to $0.339$.
   * Standalone Semantic Search still holds the highest MRR ($0.400$), nDCG@10 ($0.515$), and Evidence Completeness ($50.0\%$).
   * Neighbor expansion inserted into retrieval slots is **severely harmful**, but neighbor expansion used exclusively during **context assembly** increases required evidence recovery to **$50.0\%$**.

2. **Remaining Uncertainties**:
   * Impact of minimum cosine distance thresholding prior to fusion.
   * Scalability of vector-dominant fusion on larger, non-play corpora.

3. **Production Recommendation**:
   * **Do NOT deploy 3-parent deduplication alongside 80/20 RRF**.
   * The optimal production retrieval configuration is **80/20 RRF Hybrid Search** with **Neighbor Context Expansion ($\pm 2$) during context assembly**.

